      "body": "_Source: data-quality audit of deployment `8fcf9a8` (2026-07-07). Full findings: [Notion audit](https://app.notion.com/p/Indexer-Data-Quality-Audit-8fcf9a8-2026-07-07-3980016b2927814cb77fd6f6f8738684)._\n\n## What to build\n\nGate reward-claim USD valuation at claim time so poisoned prices cannot freeze into cumulative counters. The Base total for `totalFeeRewardClaimedUSD` ($2.27B) is roughly 87% phantom: three pools carry $1.97B created when reward tokens were valued at absurd fresh prices at claim time.\n\n- PROMPT accepted at $23,989 per token against a real value near $0.05.\n- MAMO accepted at roughly $35,000 per token.\n- LFI accepted at $7.96 against a real value of $0.000187, and this instance dates to June 2026, after the pricing hardening in #892.\n\nHealthy pools show a fee-reward-to-fees-generated ratio near 1 (voters receive the pool's swap fees). These three sit 600 to 5,900 times higher. The same mechanism inflates `totalBribeClaimedUSD`: OVN priced at $4,277 in March 2024 produced roughly $106M (34% of the Base bribe total) across three Overnight pools.\n\nUser-to-pool conservation holds exactly, so the accounting is internally consistent and the valuation is what was poisoned. The damage is cumulative and survives reindexing.\n\nRoot cause: `src/EventHandlers/VotingReward/VotingRewardSharedLogic.ts` lines 113-122 value the claim through `getTrustedUSD` with no cross-check against a plausible magnitude.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] A magnitude/plausibility check gates claim-USD at claim time (for example, reject or clamp a claim valuation whose implied fee-reward-to-fees ratio is far outside the expected band, or whose reward-token price fails a sanity check).\n- [ ] New claims for poisoned reward tokens no longer inflate `totalFeeRewardClaimedUSD` or `totalBribeClaimedUSD`.\n- [ ] User-to-pool conservation preserved.\n- [ ] Tests cover a poisoned reward-token claim and a healthy claim.\n\n## Blocked by\n\nNone — can start immediately.\n",
